## Bugs to fix

- [ ] **DAP "port error" on the second laptop.** Starting the debugger errors out. Cause is
      almost certainly a legacy `type = "executable"` codelldb adapter there — nvim-dap only
      substitutes `${port}` for `type = "server"`, so codelldb receives the literal `${port}`.
      Fix: run `scripts/setup-nvim-dap.sh` (step 3 now moves such files aside), `:Lazy sync`,
      restart. Checks + error capture: `notes/23-debug-lazyvim-troubleshoot.md`. The primary
      machine is verified clean.
- [x] **`tokenize_string` overran the source on unterminated input** — fixed 2026-11-27: the
      increment is inside the `closing_quote` branch, so the NUL exit leaves the cursor alone.
- [x] **Unknown chars now report errors** (`@`, lone `!`, …): `default:` and the lone-`!` else
      call `error_reporting`; `lone_bang_reports_error` pins the position. `notes/41` defect 7.
- [x] **`grow_list_capisity` returns `bool` and `tkn_list_add` reports OOM at the source**
      (error_msg `"out of memory"`, error_pos at the token being pushed, one stderr line).
      Callers can ignore the return because `had_error` stops the main loop. defects 2/3/4.
      OOM itself is reasoned about, not deterministically tested — see `notes/41`.
- [x] **`token_type_name` implemented 2026-11-27:** 27 enum cases, no `default:` (so `-Wswitch`
      catches a new enumerator), fallback `"UNKNOWN"` after the switch; scratch copy deleted.
- [x] **String push guard tightened 2026-11-27:** the dispatch arm now checks
      `!lexer.lex_tkn_list_struct->had_error` before `tkn_list_add`, so an unterminated string
      cannot let `tkn_list_add` overwrite `error_pos` (stays 0) or `error_msg`.
- [x] **EOF token fields fixed 2026-11-27:** `token_string = lexer.input_string +
      lexer.cursor_position`, `token_length = 0`, `source_index = lexer.cursor_position`;
      test-first assertion in `select_input_is_select_then_eof`. defect 6 closed.

