## Open design decisions (decide before the parser grows)

- [x] **OOM/error reporting — DECIDED 2026-11-26:** return the partial list with
      `had_error = true`, `error_pos` at the bad byte, `error_msg` set; caller frees. Print
      one line to stderr at the detection site; truncate the list at the bad byte with **no
      EOF** (EOF is success-only). One contract for lexical errors and allocation failure.
      The existing `errorrrr`/`return NULL` tail must be rewritten.
- [x] **`token_type_name` spelling:** enum names (`"STAR"`, `"LTE"`) chosen and documented in
      `src/tokenizer.h`; parser `expect()` messages will use those names.
- [x] **EOF token field convention** — closed 2026-11-27 (see bug above).

